    ["misc_files",
    ".FLK",
    "AccountEdge Company Lock File",
    "3.4",
    "An FLK file is a lock file used by AccountEdge Pro, an application that enables you to organize business accounting information. It secures.MYO files when multiple users are accessing the same company file. When an MYO company file is accessed by multiple AccountEdge users, the FLK file is generated in the same location as the company file. The FLK file is created to allow one user to work on the file at a time to avoid duplicate and conflicting editing. When ending a session, the FLK file is automatically deleted. However, if the session ends abruptly, the FLK file may persist. If this occurs, delete any FLK file(s) that are in the same location as the MYO company file. FLK files are not meant to be opened. They are only utilized by AccountEdge for locking MYO files. Windows Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Mac Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Encrypted locker file created by Folder Lock, a program used to protect files and folders; stores a collection of files and folders that are encrypted by the software and password-protected with a user-supplied password; protected using 256-bit AES encryption. FLK files are used for safeguarding information on computer hard drives and USB drives. They may not be deleted from computers that have Folder Lock installed. Additionally, they may only be unlocked and opened using the correct password. Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "Windows Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Mac Acclivity AccountEdge Pro. Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "?"],
    ["misc_files",
    ".CAS",
    "Autodesk Cascade License File",
    "3.4",
    "A CAS file is a license file used by Autodesk products such as AutoCAD and Revit. It contains information that validates a purchased software copy. CAS files are used in a cascading license setup, where a network installation of the software can be used by multiple networked computers. CAS files use the filename CascadeInfo.cas. These files can potentially become corrupt if the computer unexpectedly crashes, denying access to the software. If this occurs, consult Autodesk support to resolve the issue. By default, the CascadeInfo.cas file is located in the following directory: Windows Vista/7: C:/​ProgramData/​Autodesk/​ADLM/​ Windows XP: C:/​Documents and Settings/​All Users/​Application Data/​Autodesk/​ADLM/​ macOS: /​Library/​Application Support/​Autodesk/​Adlm/​.config/​. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Autodesk MEP. Autodesk Revit Structure. Autodesk AutoCAD Architecture. Mac Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. A CAS file is a 3D model used by some games in the Total War strategy game series. It may contain a model of a building, unit, or other game object. CAS files are saved with.TGA and.DDS images used for texturing the models. CAS files can be imported and exported with Autodesk 3ds Max modeling software using the Vercengetorix CAS Importer/Exporter script. Windows The Creative Assembly Total War: ROME II. Autodesk 3ds Max 2023.",
    "Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Autodesk MEP. Autodesk Revit Structure. Autodesk AutoCAD Architecture. Mac Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Windows The Creative Assembly Total War: ROME II. Autodesk 3ds Max 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["misc_files",
    ".MAR",
    "Mozilla Archive",
    "3.4",
    "Application update file used by Mozilla programs such as Firefox, Thunderbird, and SeaMonkey; contains files that update the program to a new version; run by the Mozilla update program (update.exe in Windows), which is included with Mozilla software installations; stored in a custom file format, but Mozilla has made the specification publically available. Mozilla programs automatically download and run MAR files, so the typical user will never manually open a MAR file. However, MAR files can be used to manually update a Mozilla program without opening it, which can be useful for system administrators. The Mozilla development team generates nightly builds for their software products that include a MAR update package. Therefore, users can apply software updates with the latest release each day. NOTE: MAR files created by the Mozilla team use the filename convention [program]-[version].complete.mar and [program]-[version].parial.mar for complete and partial software updates. Windows Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkey. Mac Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkey. Linux Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkeyFree. Shortcut file created by Microsoft Access, a relational database program for the desktop computer; contains a link to a report in an Access database; can be created by dragging a report object to the desktop and can be opened by double-clicking the file. Windows Microsoft Access 365. Spreadsheet created with Mariner Calc, a lightweight spreadsheet application for Mac OS X; contains data organized into rows and columns; supports functions, charts, named ranges, sorting, and auto-summation. MAR files are saved in a proprietary format that can only be opened with Mariner Calc. Mac Mariner Calc XLS. A MAR file is an archive used by MSN Explorer, an integrated web browser, email, and instant messaging client developed by Microsoft. It contains.HTM,.JS,.XSL,.GIF, and other constituent files used to load a section of MSN Explorer. For example, the file mail.mar contains files used to load MSN Explorers email functionality. MSN Explorer is an integrated Internet access application available to those who have an MSN Internet subscription. For example, MSN Explorer is available to those with MSN Dial-Up Internet Access. Microsoft integrated MSN Explorer into Windows XP. Versions of the program are also available for Windows 7, 8, and 10. The Windows XP version of MSN Explorer stores many of its core files in MAR archives. These archives, and the files they contain, are used to load various MSN Explorer features. MSN Explorers MAR files can be found in the following directory: ~/​MSN Explorer/​MSNCoreFiles. mail.mar - Contains files used by MSN Explorers Mail feature. ui.mar - Contains MSN Explorer UI elements. MAR files are not meant to be opened. However, you can use brzs MarEx extraction tool (Windows) to extract the files a MAR file contains. You can also use MarEx to pack files into a MAR file. Windows Microsoft MSN Explorer. brz MarExFree.",
    "Windows Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkey. Mac Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkey. Linux Mozilla Firefox. Mozilla Thunderbird. Mozilla SeaMonkey. Windows Microsoft Access 365. Mac Mariner Calc XLS. Windows Microsoft MSN Explorer. brz MarEx.",
    "?"],
    ["misc_files",
    ".RPMSG",
    "Outlook Restricted Permission Message",
    "3.4",
    "An RPMSG file is a protected email message created by Microsoft Outlook, Microsofts email and calendar application. It contains an email that has been encrypted such that only certain users can view, print, copy, or forward it. RPMSG files are sent as attachments to standard email messages; these attachments use the filename message.rpmsg. Outlook users can use the programs information rights management (IRM) features to protect emails they send. When a user protects an email this way, Outlook compresses and encrypts the messages contents, as well as any permissions the sender has specified (e.g. restrictions on forwarding or printing the message). It then saves this encrypted version of the message as an RPMSG file. The RPMSG file is sent to recipients as an attachment to a normal Outlook message. The message explains it contains protected content, and it includes a link that can be used to open the RPMSG file. Only specified recipients can open RPMSG files. NOTE: Azure Information Protection also creates encrypted email messages saved as RPMSG files. message.rpmsg - The standard name of RPMSG files; included as attachments in email messages. In Microsoft Outlook and other email applications, you can open a protected email message by clicking the message.rpmsg file attached to an email. When using an application other than Outlook, you may be redirected to a separate webpage to view the protected message. Keep in mind that you can open a protected message only while logged in to an email account to which the message was originally sent. Windows Microsoft Outlook 365. Microsoft Azure Information Protection Viewer. Mac Apple Mail Included with OS. Microsoft Outlook 365. Web Gmail. iOS Apple Mail Included with OS. Android GmailFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft Outlook 365. Microsoft Azure Information Protection Viewer. Mac Apple Mail Included with OS. Microsoft Outlook 365. Web Gmail. iOS Apple Mail Included with OS. Android Gmail.",
    "?"],
    ["misc_files",
    ".LID",
    "Kodak EasyShare Album File",
    "3.4",
    "Stores album information for photos and videos captured with a Kodak EasyShare camera; defines what album each photo or video is stored in; used to organize and keep track of different sets of photos and videos. LID files are used by the EasyShare software included with the camera. They are saved in the same directory as the image files, but do not contain actual image data. NOTE: Kodak discontinued the development of the EasyShare program. Windows Kodak EasyShare Mac Kodak EasyShare Linux UNIX Kodak EasyShare tools.",
    "Windows Kodak EasyShare. Mac Kodak EasyShare. Linux UNIX Kodak EasyShare tools.",
    "?"],
